<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Magdalena River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Magdalena is the principal river of Colombia, flowing about 1,500 km north between the Central and Eastern Cordilleras to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> near Barranquilla. Spanish expeditions, including that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-jimenez-de-quesada">Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada</a> in 1536, used it to reach the Andean interior and the lands of the Muisca. For centuries it was the main route between the Caribbean coast and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/magdalena-river.jpg" alt="Magdalena River" width="320" height="294" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexrk2 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rio_Magdalena_Delta_landsat.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
